# ApexPost.Api requests (Part B, unversioned /api/v2/shipments).
# Works in Visual Studio 2022 (Endpoints Explorer), VS Code (REST Client) and Rider.
# Run the API first:  dotnet run --project .\ApexPost.Api --launch-profile https
# Requests run top to bottom. Each request has one success case and one failure case.

@host = https://localhost:7153
@tn = APX-10000001
@scanA = 3f2b8c1e-6a4d-4e0b-9a51-7d1c2e8f4b10
@scanB = 8c1d0f55-2b7e-4a39-b1c6-0e5a9d3f7a22

### 1. Create a shipment -> 201 Created + Location header
POST {{host}}/api/v2/shipments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trackingNumber": "{{tn}}",
  "recipientName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "recipientPhone": "+61 400 000 111",
  "address": "12 Example Street",
  "city": "Melbourne",
  "weightKg": 2.5
}

### 1b. Create, FAILURE -> 400 ValidationProblemDetails (bad tracking number, weight out of range, missing fields)
POST {{host}}/api/v2/shipments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trackingNumber": "BAD-1",
  "recipientName": "",
  "weightKg": 100
}

### 1c. Create, FAILURE -> 409 Conflict (run request 1 twice)
POST {{host}}/api/v2/shipments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trackingNumber": "{{tn}}",
  "recipientName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "recipientPhone": "+61 400 000 111",
  "address": "12 Example Street",
  "city": "Melbourne",
  "weightKg": 2.5
}

### 1d. Create, FAILURE -> 415 Unsupported Media Type
POST {{host}}/api/v2/shipments
Content-Type: text/plain

trackingNumber=APX-10000009

### 2. List shipments (paged, filtered) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v2/shipments?page=1&pageSize=20&status=Created&city=Melbourne

### 2b. List, FAILURE -> 400 (unknown status)
GET {{host}}/api/v2/shipments?status=Teleported

### 3. Get one shipment -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/{{tn}}

### 3b. Get, FAILURE -> 404 (unknown tracking number)
GET {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/APX-99999999

### 4. Replace editable details -> 200 (only while status is Created)
PUT {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/{{tn}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipientName": "Grace Hopper",
  "recipientPhone": "0400 000 333",
  "address": "9 New Lane",
  "city": "Sydney",
  "weightKg": 4
}

### 4b. Replace, FAILURE -> 400 (weight out of range)
PUT {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/{{tn}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipientName": "Grace Hopper",
  "recipientPhone": "0400 000 333",
  "address": "9 New Lane",
  "city": "Sydney",
  "weightKg": 0.01
}

### 5. Change status (next step only) -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/{{tn}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "PickedUp" }

### 5b. Change status, FAILURE -> 409 (skips InTransit and OutForDelivery)
PATCH {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/{{tn}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Delivered" }

### 6. Upload scans (idempotent: send it twice, the second response says duplicatesSkipped) -> 200
POST {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/{{tn}}/scans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scans": [
    { "scanId": "{{scanA}}", "scanType": "Arrived", "location": "Melbourne Depot", "scannedAtUtc": "2026-11-08T22:00:00Z" },
    { "scanId": "{{scanB}}", "scanType": "Departed", "location": "Melbourne Depot", "scannedAtUtc": "2026-11-08T23:00:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 6b. Upload scans, FAILURE -> 400 (Delivered scan without a signature name, and a scan in the future)
POST {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/{{tn}}/scans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scans": [
    { "scanId": "5a0c7e91-3d44-4b6f-8e12-9f7b6c1d2a33", "scanType": "Delivered", "location": "12 Example Street", "scannedAtUtc": "2026-11-08T23:30:00Z" },
    { "scanId": "6b1d8fa2-4e55-4c70-9f23-a08c7d2e3b44", "scanType": "Arrived", "location": "Melbourne Depot", "scannedAtUtc": "2099-01-01T00:00:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 7. Scan history -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/{{tn}}/scans

### 7b. Scan history, FAILURE -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/APX-99999999/scans

### 8. Delete (only while status is Created). Create APX-10000002 first, then delete it -> 204
POST {{host}}/api/v2/shipments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trackingNumber": "APX-10000002",
  "recipientName": "Alan Turing",
  "recipientPhone": "0390001234",
  "address": "1 Demo Road",
  "city": "Melbourne",
  "weightKg": 1
}

###
DELETE {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/APX-10000002

### 8b. Delete, FAILURE -> 409 (the shipment was picked up in request 5)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/{{tn}}


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Part C: versions, headers and contracts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 9. v2 shipment: nested "recipient", "latestScan" and "status" as a string -> 200
# Look at the response headers too: api-supported-versions: 2.0 and api-deprecated-versions: 1.0
GET {{host}}/api/v2/shipments/{{tn}}

### 10. v1 (DEPRECATED) shipment: flat recipient fields and a NUMERIC status (0 = Created ... 5 = Failed) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/shipments/{{tn}}

### 10b. v1 list -> 200 (same paging rules, flat items)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/shipments?page=1&pageSize=20

### 10c. v1 create -> 201, Location is /api/v1/shipments/APX-10000003
POST {{host}}/api/v1/shipments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trackingNumber": "APX-10000003",
  "recipientName": "Grace Hopper",
  "recipientPhone": "0400 000 333",
  "address": "9 New Lane",
  "city": "Sydney",
  "weightKg": 3
}

### 10d. v1 scan upload: the scan contract is the same in both versions -> 200
POST {{host}}/api/v1/shipments/APX-10000003/scans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scans": [
    { "scanId": "7c2e9ab3-5f66-4d81-a034-b19d8e3f4c55", "scanType": "PickedUp", "location": "Sydney Depot", "scannedAtUtc": "2026-11-08T21:00:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 11. FAILURE -> 404: the old unversioned route no longer exists
GET {{host}}/api/shipments/{{tn}}

### 12. OpenAPI contract of each version (Development only)
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json

###
GET {{host}}/openapi/v2.json

### 13. Swagger UI (open in a browser, Development only): {{host}}/swagger
